{"name":"Devon Rex","hex":"#717e6f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Devon Rex","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A domestic cat of a particular medium-sized breed with rippled or swirling hair, originated in Britain in the 1960s."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Devon_Rex"}],"entries":[{"title":"Devon Rex","blocks":[{"text":"The Devon Rex is a tall-eared, short-haired breed of cat that emerged in England during the late 1950s. The breed is known for its atypical appearance, with an oddly shaped head, large eyes, and the short and wavy coat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Devon_Rex_Cassini.jpeg/330px-Devon_Rex_Cassini.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devon_Rex","wikidata":"Q42570"},{"title":"Devon","blocks":[{"text":"Devon is a ceremonial county in South West England. It is bordered by the Bristol Channel to the north, Somerset and Dorset to the east, the English Channel to the south, and Cornwall to the west. The city of Plymouth is the largest settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Dartmoor_ponies_by_the_B3212_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4546147.jpg/330px-Dartmoor_ponies_by_the_B3212_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4546147.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devon","wikidata":"Q23156"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg/250px-Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg/500px-Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg/250px-Saucer-eyed_Devon_Rex.jpg?utm_so